    {
      "topLeftX": 247,
      "topLeftY": 61,
      "bottomRightX": 491,
      "bottomRightY": 90,
      "content": "# Language review 3",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 102,
      "bottomRightX": 250,
      "bottomRightY": 120,
      "content": "### *1 Use of the Passive*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 131,
      "bottomRightX": 613,
      "bottomRightY": 165,
      "content": "You use the Passive when you want to make the thing done more important than the person who does it.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 179,
      "bottomRightX": 519,
      "bottomRightY": 246,
      "content": "**Examples:** The doctors let Ed Shaw out of hospital. →\nEd Shaw **was let out** of hospital.\nThe police arrested a man for dangerous driving. →\nA man **was arrested** for dangerous driving.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 268,
      "bottomRightX": 316,
      "bottomRightY": 285,
      "content": "### *2 Use of the Past continuous*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 296,
      "bottomRightX": 576,
      "bottomRightY": 314,
      "content": "You use the Past continuous when you want to set the scene for a story.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 326,
      "bottomRightX": 570,
      "bottomRightY": 361,
      "content": "**Examples:** We were working in the fields (when something happened).\n**Note:** Use the Past simple to say *what happened*, e.g. *I heard somebody*.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 375,
      "bottomRightX": 494,
      "bottomRightY": 411,
      "content": "### *3 Sense verbs (hear, see, feel) followed by an object then a verb.*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 425,
      "bottomRightX": 481,
      "bottomRightY": 443,
      "content": "You can use these structure to continue the scene-setting.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 455,
      "bottomRightX": 437,
      "bottomRightY": 490,
      "content": "**Examples:** I heard somebody. He was shouting. →\nI heard somebody shouting.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 502,
      "bottomRightX": 359,
      "bottomRightY": 520,
      "content": "### *4 The verb to be + to + infinitive*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 532,
      "bottomRightX": 616,
      "bottomRightY": 567,
      "content": "You can use these structure to talk about future plans or forecasts. You often see it in newspaper.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 582,
      "bottomRightX": 515,
      "bottomRightY": 616,
      "content": "**Examples:** The President **is to meet** the ambassador tomorrow.\nThe thick fog **is to clear** this afternoon.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 629,
      "bottomRightX": 219,
      "bottomRightY": 647,
      "content": "### *5 Punctuation*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 658,
      "bottomRightX": 583,
      "bottomRightY": 693,
      "content": "In newspaper reports the writer uses a mixture of direct and reported speech for variety and interest.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 90,
      "topLeftY": 707,
      "bottomRightX": 581,
      "bottomRightY": 804,
      "content": "These are called speech marks.\n'It's a miracle they were found,' a Rescue Service spokesman said. 'We can't explain it.'\nNote the comma here.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 853,
      "bottomRightX": 551,
      "bottomRightY": 873,
      "content": "**Find other examples of the above language in the texts.**",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 88,
      "topLeftY": 883,
      "bottomRightX": 477,
      "bottomRightY": 902,
      "content": "**Now do activities A, B, and C in the Workbook.**",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
